module main

-- §4.5 SOUNDNESS (NEGATIVE, 6th hole — a COMPOSITION, not a free RESULT):
-- '__runIO : forall e a. IO e a -> a' is an 'unsafePerformIO' — it extracts an
-- 'IO e a' result PURELY, DISCARDING the error channel. Its own result 'a' is
-- pinned to the argument, so the original free-RESULT door-survey excluded it;
-- but 'throwIO : forall e a. e -> IO e a' produces an 'IO e a' with a FREE 'a'
-- (sound — the IO value never yields an 'a'). The composition
-- '__runIO (throwIO Unit)' therefore has a free result type and type-checks at
-- ANY proposition: 'let bad : (=) True False = __runIO (throwIO Unit)' forges a
-- false equation, and 'subst' over a discriminator family then inhabits 'Void':
-- total logical unsoundness. The program ENTRY does not need '__runIO' (the
-- runtime drives 'main' directly), and the §18.3.1 monadic splice '!e' desugars
-- to a monadic BIND ('tmp <- e'), NOT a '__runIO e' extraction — so no
-- synthesized '__runIO' term reaches this gate. Gating the USER-direct name is
-- therefore sound: a plain module naming '__runIO' is rejected.

bad : (=) True False
let bad = __runIO (throwIO Unit)

--! assertDiagnostic error E_UNSAFE_INTRINSIC_GATED
